[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=kldload — build in progress
Comment=Window showing that the post-install build is still running
# WHY THIS AUTOSTARTS FOR EVERY USER:
#
# A kldload install reaches a usable desktop long before it is finished.
# kldload-firstboot is still pulling models and building kernel modules, and
# kldload-autodeploy then builds golden VMs and bootstraps a cluster — its unit
# allows six hours. A desktop that looks finished while multi-GB work continues
# invites exactly one action, and it is the wrong one.
#
# HISTORY: 2026-08-13. A user saw the desktop, assumed the install was done,
# and rebooted mid-build. firstboot's ExecStartPost never ran, so it started
# over on the next boot, and kldload-rag.service — enabled but with no model
# pulled yet — began respawning every five seconds. Nothing had failed; it had
# been interrupted, and nothing on screen had said not to.
#
# The wrapper exits immediately and opens no window once /var/lib/kldload/
# all-ready exists, so on a finished machine this costs one process spawn at
# login and nothing else.
Exec=/usr/local/bin/kldload-build-monitor-autostart
Terminal=false
NoDisplay=true
# DISABLED 2026-08-23, at the operator's request: on a workstation the window
# at every login was more nuisance than warning. Flip this back to true to
# restore it — the wrapper and its unit are untouched, and `kldload-buildmon`
# still runs on demand, so nothing is lost but the automatic appearance.
#
# KNOW WHAT THIS GIVES UP: the incident above. Nothing on screen will now say
# the build is still running, so a machine that looks finished can be rebooted
# mid-build again. `cat /var/lib/kldload/current-phase` answers it, and the
# absence of /var/lib/kldload/all-ready is the same signal this used to show.
X-GNOME-Autostart-enabled=false
# NO X-GNOME-Autostart-Phase HERE. It used to say `Applications`, to land late
# enough in the login sequence that a terminal emulator was available. On
# GNOME 48 (Fedora 44) that key does not merely get ignored — the entry is
# SKIPPED. gnome-session logs it and moves on:
#
#   gnome-session-service: App kldload-build-monitor.desktop sets
#   X-GNOME-Autostart-Phase, but gnome-session no longer manages session
#   services
#
# so the monitor never launched on a Fedora desktop, and the operator reached
# a finished-looking desktop with a multi-GB build still running behind it —
# the exact failure this autostart exists to prevent. The four entries without
# the key (kldload-webui, nvidia-settings-user, ...) started normally in the
# same login, which is what made it obvious. (.105, 2026-08-17.)
#
# The phase key was never load-bearing anyway: the wrapper exits quietly when
# no terminal emulator is present, and the GUI path it prefers needs none.
